While the many digits don't convey much information, the
relative size of the numbers do.  In the +0 column the numbers
go from 15 for Mojo to 3 for Sting.  It tells me which artifacts
matter the most early on, and which matter most later on.
If I have a choice and need damage I should pick higher on the
list if I think the number difference matters - I think 15 vs 3
matters but I might not think 12 vs 11 matters.

The change in order between the two lists is instructive -
Given the choice I might use an artifact that is high on the
second list even in the early game in order to acquire the
maximum skill in it.  It also shows that double damage
against most monsters counts a lot.

Position relative to how easy it is to acquire is also instructive.
The low position of Sting says the reason to name it has
almost nothing to do with the damage it does and is only
about skills and other features.  The relatively high position
of Orcrist reminds me that elven broadsword is a better
non-artifact weapon than I normally pay attention to.

Interesting - Most of the guaranteed first gifts to combat
wombats are interleaved with the crowning gifts on both
lists.  To me this means they are all enough for ascension.
And the low damage from magicbane says the same thing
as the low damage from Sting - It is about something other
than melee damage.



